%% Claim submission — two-phase, asynchronous processing, and failure handling
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Customer
  participant App as Mobile app
  participant DB as SQLite (device)
  participant API as Claims API
  participant PG as Postgres
  participant S3 as Object storage
  participant Q as Queue (SQS)
  participant W as Worker
  participant DLQ as DLQ
  participant L as Legacy system

  Note over App,L: one correlationId (W3C traceparent) spans every hop

  U->>App: fill wizard, tap Submit
  App->>DB: tx: draft + clientClaimId + outbox item
  App->>API: POST /v1/claims (payload + document manifest)
  API->>PG: tx: claims + outbox_events + document metadata
  API-->>App: 201 reference + presigned URLs
  App-->>U: "Submitted · NW-2026-000123"
  loop each document
    App->>S3: PUT object (progress)
    App->>API: POST /claims/{id}/documents/{docId}/complete
    API->>S3: HeadObject (size/type validation)
    API-->>App: 200 uploaded
  end
  PG->>Q: publisher moves outbox event
  Q->>W: message (at-least-once)
  W->>L: createClaim(reference, idempotency key)
  alt legacy down
    W-->>W: breaker opens, retry with backoff
    Note over W,L: no submission is lost
  else legacy ok
    L-->>W: legacy claim number
    W->>PG: append legacy_accepted to timeline
    W->>App: notification hint (push / inbox)
  else legacy rejects permanently
    Q->>DLQ: after N attempts
    Note over DLQ: listed for operator redrive; nothing silently lost
  end
